    "category": "llm-ai",
    "subcategory": "debug-leakage",
    "title": "OTEL debug logging enabled — leaks prompts, thinking, tool parameters, and tool results",
    "description": "Claude Code OTEL debug-logging env vars emit sensitive content as OpenTelemetry log events / span attributes. OTEL_LOG_RAW_API_BODIES=1 (v2.1.111+) emits full request and response bodies (prompts, thinking, assistant responses). OTEL_LOG_TOOL_DETAILS=1 (v2.1.101+) logs tool parameters into spans — and since v2.1.157 also into tool_decision events — exposing Bash command lines, Write/Edit file paths and contents, and any secret passed as a tool argument. OTEL_LOG_TOOL_CONTENT=1 logs full tool results (file contents, command output, query results). OTEL_LOG_USER_PROMPTS=1 emits user_system_prompt and user_prompt span/event content (full user prompts and the system prompt, plus slash-command names and sources) — direct leakage of user input and instructions. In production telemetry pipelines or any backend routed to a SaaS observability platform, enabling any of these is a confidentiality breach. Designed for local debugging only. OTEL_LOG_ASSISTANT_RESPONSES=1 (v2.1.193+) de-redacts the claude_code.assistant_response log event, which carries the model's full response text; when the variable is unset it inherits OTEL_LOG_USER_PROMPTS, so enabling prompt logging silently enables response logging too. CLAUDE_CODE_OTEL_CONTENT_MAX_LENGTH (v2.1.214+) raises the 60 KB truncation cap on OTel content attributes — a large or disabled cap turns truncated leakage into complete leakage.",
    "detect": {
      "patterns": [
