scripts/pattern-gen.py-154-Rules:
scripts/pattern-gen.py-155-- Patterns are Python-compatible regex strings used with re.search() on source code lines
scripts/pattern-gen.py-156-- Patterns should be specific enough to detect the vulnerability class, not just the CVE product
scripts/pattern-gen.py-157-- Focus on the CWE (weakness class) to write general patterns, not product-specific strings
scripts/pattern-gen.py:158:- negative_patterns are strings/regexes that indicate the vulnerability is mitigated (e.g., sanitization functions)
scripts/pattern-gen.py-159-- file_types are glob patterns for files to scan (e.g., "*.js", "*.py", "*.go")
scripts/pattern-gen.py-160-- exclude lists directory names to skip during scanning
scripts/pattern-gen.py-161-- confidence: 1.0 = exact CVE pattern, 0.7 = CWE-class pattern, 0.4 = broad heuristic
scripts/pattern-gen.py-162-- If the CVE is too product-specific or infrastructure-only (no detectable code pattern), \
--
