   292	      "description": "Claude Code sandbox settings that reduce the isolation applied to sandboxed commands. sandbox.filesystem.disabled=true (v2.1.216+) skips filesystem isolation entirely while keeping only network egress control, so a sandboxed command regains full read/write access to the host tree. sandbox.network.strictAllowlist=false (v2.1.219+) lets sandboxed commands reach hosts that are not on the allowlist without prompting, defeating egress control and enabling silent exfiltration. sandbox.credentials configured to permit credential access lets sandboxed commands read credential files and secret environment variables (v2.1.187+ added the setting precisely to block this). sandbox.allowAppleEvents=true (v2.1.181+) lets sandboxed commands drive other macOS applications via Apple Events — a sandbox escape by proxy. Each of these is legitimate as a deliberate, scoped, local choice; committed to a repo, a Dockerfile, CI config, or managed settings, they silently strip the isolation that the rest of the posture assumes.",
